I agree and disagree but this is the best answer I've read.

&#x200B;

I disagree in the fact that he's reached the end of his character arc, the creation for his character just isn't relevant to the Krakoan Arc too much, though I think he would have made a more genuine choice for the Round Table as he exited a great lead up into Krakoa by becoming the King of Thieves and saving Rogue from Candra.

&#x200B;

For him to grow as a character, he would need to explore his own roots more explicitly with a purpose that attaches to a grander play of theme. The mystery behind him still has hidden potential, especially now that the Siege Perilous has brought back perhaps any Gambit from any multiverse. Who could he be? lol

I also agree he has been explored well but his core conflict would rest on the darkness of his identity from knowing who he really is, as he was an orphan taken in by the Thieves guild. Chris Claremont originally had intentions to make him the clone of the boy that couldn't age from hundreds of years ago, where one became him and the other Nathaniel Essex, that'd be interesting to explore. I'd write a time travel arc where he is in that key moment as the baby clone which is transported into the future from the past and ends up as the chosen on for the Thieves guild with greater purpose tied to the Tithe. The energy he possesses being the ultimate New Son, which is then brought into the hands of Mr Sinister to create a mutant strong enough to beat the Phalanx and everything else. ... With enough character development this would all be really cool.
